{
  "name": "ux-mcpp",
  "description": "0.0.7 plan 6.4 (U1-U15): the user-experience scenario tests on the mcpp repository at the commit self-mcpp pins (176 modules), on the CI runner's size (4 vCPU: run under taskset -c 0-3). One scenario, five runs selected by --stage: cold (no cache: U1 first responses, U3, U4, U14, preparation time) then warm (--expect-warm, the same --cache-dir: U2) then edits (the warm cache: U5-U8 typing, fan-out saves, build-graph changes), faults (a cache of its own: U9-U11 kill clangd, kill the server, stale locks, a truncated module file) and long (nightly only: U13 ten idle minutes and U12 a git checkout twenty commits back and forth). Every stage ends with U15's timeline. The budgets are the plan's initial values (6.4), calibrated on the first rounds of the 4-vCPU CI runner (PR #33, 2026-09-30; plan 6.4 and 13 say why each changed): documentSymbol and semanticTokens need clangd's AST of the file, so they are held to the server's request timeout, not to 1 s (the editor colours with the TextMate grammar meanwhile); cold preparation, the first clangd answers, a warm start's first jump, the refresh of diagnostics after typing and the recovery from a stale lock to what the runner measured over two rounds, which differed by up to 1.9x on the same runner type, with a margin; completion by clangd at 75% (the 1 s budget on a large file typed at 10 Hz), and U7a's interactive p95 at 1.5 s, since a request clangd cannot answer while eight importers rebuild is answered by mcppls at its 1 s budget; an autosaved half-typed import sets its file aside until it is saved again (fix plan F16), and one ending in '.' spins clangd's scan of the file on disk (issue #24 UP-01, UP-14) until clangd is restarted -- once typing pauses, at most a minute later -- so U6 allows both; U7b is in the nightly stage while clangd crashes on that save (issue #24 UP-20); the faults stage restarts clangd or the server on purpose five times, each a walk from starting to ready, so its timeline allows twelve state changes a minute like the edits stage; a budget is tightened as measured rounds allow and loosened only with its reason written here; U1's first clangd answers are asked in every round of U4's cold phase, in the same window as its requests; the checks measure everything they name, budgeted or not, into --measure. Run it with --log-level debug (the fixture passes it) so that 'Built module' lines can be counted.",
